{
 "about": "Front FR0: the fr glossary (plan analysis/front-plans/front-i18n-fr.md §5) that src/i18n/fr/fr.test.ts enforces through the SC4 lint framework (src/i18n/lint/, profile fr) on every French string. Seeded from the Portuguese glossary: the same English patterns and interface names, re-targeted to French from the English (Spanish and Portuguese only as meaning context) and the IAU Office of Astronomy for Education French glossary. A term applies when its English pattern matches the English source: the French must then match the `fr` stem or pattern. Names are fixed interface names (an exact name applies only to a whole string; the name match ignores case). Forbidden here are the term forms this glossary rejects (ligne for a spectral line, cluster, redshift, supporté for supported); the language-wide rules (typography with the typographic apostrophe and guillemets, the vous register and the tu-forms it rejects, elision, Spanish and Portuguese words left from the context languages, anglicisms and false friends, claims that a translation is CLEA's or official) live in the fr profile of src/i18n/lint/profiles.ts. VIREO's own names follow the brief's decided forms (Save → Enregistrer, Record → Consigner, Find → Localiser, Search → Rechercher, Show → Afficher, Display → Affichage, Slew → Déplacer, Init/Go → Préparer/Démarrer, Scan → Faire défiler, Clear → Effacer, Reset → Réinitialiser, Hot List → liste d’objets, lab → TP). Rows for areas still in English wait for their sub-front (FR1–FR6). Translations are web adaptations by OpenVireo, never CLEA's.",
